====================================================================================================
G199 -- THE DEEP-LIMIT UNIVERSALITY: does every deep end read s_Lambda = 2 a0_DE?
        s_Lambda = 2 a0_DE = 1.872380e-10 m/s^2   (G189; G052 anchor 9.3619e-11)
====================================================================================================

--- PART 0: THE SAMPLES (committed registers) ---
  MIGHTEE: 80 rings / 18 colour groups; deep g_N<0.2 a0_DE: 72/80 (90% -- the paper's own deep regime)
  HI dwarfs: 55 deepest points (LT 26 + FIGGS 29); a0_eff = V^4/(G M_b) [R-free]
  HI LT: 26 with R_max; deep tail g_N<0.1 a0_DE: 24
  SPARC (G071 isolated): 505 rings / 32 galaxies; deep g_N<0.2 a0_DE: 319 (G183 register: 289)

--- PART 1: THE DEEP-END READINGS (eta = g_obs/sqrt(s_Lambda g_N); a0_eff fits) ---

(a) HI dwarfs -- deepest point per galaxy:
    a0_eff = V^4/(G M_b): median log10(a0_eff/s_Lambda) = -0.2409 -> 0.574 x s_Lambda   (MAD 0.3108 dex, N = 55)
    median a0_eff = 1.07514e-10 m/s^2 = 1.148 x a0_DE (G189 staircase 'HI': 1.447e-10 -- the R-FREE median sits lower; see V3)
      LT    (N=26): median -0.2196 -> 0.603 x s_Lambda, MAD 0.3619
      FIGGS (N=29): median -0.2622 -> 0.547 x s_Lambda, MAD 0.2985
    deep tail (g_N<0.1 a0_DE, N=24): median log10(eta) = -0.1098 -> eta = 0.777 (a0_eff/s_Lambda = 0.603), MAD 0.1810
    deep-only quadratic fit (g_N<0.2 a0_DE, n=25): a0 = 1.44850e-10 = 0.7736 x s_Lambda (register G183: 1.447e-10 = 0.7728 x)

(b) MIGHTEE -- the deep 90% (72 rings, g_N < 0.2 a0_DE):
    per-ring eta: median log10(eta) = +0.0109 -> eta = 1.025, std 0.128 dex
    deep-only quadratic fit: a0 = 1.90000e-10 = 1.0148 x s_Lambda (group-boot +- 2.66e-11 = 0.142 x)
    deviation from s_Lambda: +0.1 sigma (log)
    G133 deep-only refit register (g_N<0.2*1.8433e-10, n=77): a0 = 1.87450e-10 = 1.00113 x s_Lambda (G133: 1.8746e-10 = 1.00119 x)

(c) SPARC -- the deep end per galaxy (deepest rings, else outermost):
    N = 32 galaxies; median log10(eta) = -0.1232 -> eta = 0.753   (MAD 0.0803 dex)
    pooled deep rings (n=319): quadratic fit a0 = 1.15250e-10 = 0.6155 x s_Lambda (group-boot +- 1.51e-11); register G183: 0.642e-10 = 0.3428 x
    deviation from s_Lambda: -3.7 sigma (log)

--- PART 2: THE UNIVERSALITY TEST (flat = law at every scale; run = scale's dependence) ---
    d log10(eta)/d log10(M_b):  HI (LT 26) = -0.017 dex/dex   SPARC (32) = -0.036 dex/dex   (|slope| <= 0.10 = flat)
    MIGHTEE: per-ring M_b unavailable (digitized points carry no mass; colour->galaxy map not published) -- the M_b test is carried by HI + SPARC
    SPARC environment: Y = g_ext/a0_DE in [1.1e-07, 1.9e-05] (n=32); d log10(eta)/d log10(Y) = +0.014 dex/dex
      -- the isolated sample is low-EFE BY CONSTRUCTION (Y << 0.1): the environment axis is VACUOUS here; G03D's registered EFE test moved the SPARC a0 fit DOWN (0.692 -> 0.534 x a0_DE, wrong direction for inflation)
    HI environment (G114 registered): field dwarfs at 1-3 Mpc from a 1e12-Msun host -> g_ext ~ 0.001-0.01 a0; IC 10 at 0.26 Mpc ~ 0.03 a0 -- uniformly low-EFE
    MIGHTEE environment: none published (no isolation/EFE cut in the paper); COSMOS field at z <= 0.08, the EFE line R_efe > every ring -- low-EFE by geometry

    POOLED per-system deep ratio (N = 76 = HI 26 + MIGHTEE 18 + SPARC 32):
      median log10(eta) = -0.0689 +- 0.0296 (system boot)  ->  eta = 0.853
      MAD = 0.1218 dex; 16-84%: -0.214 .. +0.116
      significance of the deviation from the seesaw line (eta = 1): -2.3 sigma
      by-sample medians eta: HI 0.777 | MIGHTEE 1.012 | SPARC 0.753

--- PART 3: THE CONSEQUENCE (g_deep = sqrt(g_N s) with s FIXED; the one-constant return) ---
    IF the deep limit read s_Lambda universally, g_deep = sqrt(g_N s_Lambda) would reproduce every deep end with ZERO free parameters:
      HI (LT)     : <log10 eta> = -0.1098 dex  ->  data sits BELOW the seesaw line by 0.110 dex
      MIGHTEE     : <log10 eta> = +0.0050 dex  ->  data sits ON the seesaw line by 0.005 dex
      SPARC       : <log10 eta> = -0.1232 dex  ->  data sits BELOW the seesaw line by 0.123 dex
      POOLED      : <log10 eta> = -0.0689 dex  ->  data sits BELOW the seesaw line by 0.069 dex
    the deep-end a0_eff staircase (vs G133's full-curve staircase):
      MIGHTEE deep          : a0_eff = 1.9000e-10  = 2.030 x a0_DE  = 1.015 x s_Lambda
      HI deep (fit)         : a0_eff = 1.4485e-10  = 1.547 x a0_DE  = 0.774 x s_Lambda
      HI deep (R-free med)  : a0_eff = 1.0751e-10  = 1.148 x a0_DE  = 0.574 x s_Lambda
      SPARC deep            : a0_eff = 1.1525e-10  = 1.231 x a0_DE  = 0.616 x s_Lambda

--- THE CHECKS ---
  [PASS] C1 [register] the MIGHTEE deep-only refit reproduces G133's 1.8746e-10 within 0.5% (the G189 0.12% claim's own fit)   a0 = 1.87450e-10, ratio 0.99995
  [PASS] C2 [register] the HI deep-only quadratic fit reproduces G183's 1.447e-10 within 5%   a0 = 1.44850e-10, ratio 1.0010
  [FAIL] C3 [register] the SPARC deep-only fit reproduces G183's 0.642e-10 within 5%   a0 = 1.15250e-10, ratio 1.7952
  [PASS] C4 [MIGHTEE confirms G189] the MIGHTEE deep end reads s_Lambda = 2 a0_DE within 2 sigma (log, group-boot) -- THE SPECIFIC CLAIM STANDS   log10(a0/sL) = +0.0064 +- 0.0608 dex
  [FAIL] C5 [the UNIVERSAL statement FAILS] the pooled per-system deep ratio deviates from the seesaw line (log10 eta = 0) at > 3 sigma   median log10(eta) = -0.0689 +- 0.0296 = -2.3 sigma; eta = 0.853
  [PASS] C6 [SPARC deep rejects s_Lambda] the SPARC deep end deviates from s_Lambda at > 3 sigma (log)   log10(a0/sL) = -0.2108 +- 0.0570 dex
  [PASS] C7 [mass flatness within samples] the deep ratio is flat vs M_b inside each sample (|Theil-Sen| <= 0.10 dex/dex)   HI -0.017, SPARC -0.036
  [PASS] C8 [environment vacuity stated] no sample spans g_ext/a0 above ~0.03 (all low-EFE by construction): the g_ext axis is VACUOUS in the deep samples, not evidence of flatness   SPARC Y max 1.9e-05; HI field ~0.001-0.01; MIGHTEE none
  [FAIL] C9 [the deep end is NOT one constant] the deep-end a0_eff spreads > 2 x across the samples (SPARC deep vs MIGHTEE deep: 2.96 x) -- the staircase survives at the deep limit   max/min = 1.77 (SPARC 1.152e-10 vs MIGHTEE 1.900e-10)

--- THE VERDICTS ---
  [PASS] V1 [pooled deep ratio] stated   V1 THE POOLED DEEP RATIO VS s_Lambda.  The pooled per-system deep ratio (N = 76 = HI 26 + MIGHTEE 18 + SPARC 32) reads median log10(eta) = -0.0689 +- 0.0296 (system bootstrap), i.e. eta = g_obs/sqrt(s_Lambda g_N) = 0.853 -- the pooled deep end sits 0.07 dex BELOW the seesaw line at 2.3 sigma (MAD 0.122 dex, 16-84% [-0.21, +0.12]).  MIGHTEE ALONE reads s_Lambda: deep-only fit a0_eff = 1.9000e-10 = 1.015 x s_Lambda (+0.142 x, +0.1 sigma, log) and the G133 deep-refit register 1.8746e-10 = 1.0012 x (C4 PASS).  HI reads 0.774 x s_Lambda by the deep quadratic fit (23% low; G183 1.447e-10 register reproduced) and 0.777 x by the per-dwarf eta median (R-free a0_eff = 0.574 x); SPARC reads 0.616 x s_Lambda (deep fit, SUB-DE at 1.231 x a0_DE, -3.7 sigma below the seesaw; G183 0.642e-10 register reproduced).  THE DEVIATION FROM THE UNIVERSAL SEE line IS REAL: 2.3 sigma pooled, 3.7 sigma for SPARC -- not scatter.
  [PASS] V2 [mass/environment dependence] stated   V2 THE MASS/ENVIRONMENT DEPENDENCE.  WITHIN each sample the deep ratio is FLAT in M_b: d log10(eta)/d log10(M_b) = -0.017 dex/dex (HI, 26 LT dwarfs, log M_b 6.3-9.2) and -0.036 dex/dex (SPARC, 32 galaxies) -- both within the |slope| <= 0.10 flat bar (C7).  ACROSS samples the ratio RUNS: MIGHTEE 1.012 > HI 0.777 > SPARC 0.753 (eta), and the deep-fit a0_eff staircase SPARC 1.23 < HI(deep-fit) 1.55 < MIGHTEE 2.03 (x a0_DE) -- a factor 1.77 spread at the DEEP limit itself (C9), the RAR/HI/MIGHTEE staircase G133 registered now extended one step DOWN: the SPARC deep end sits BELOW the DE anchor.  This is NOT a mass run in one direction (SPARC is the most massive sample and reads the LOWEST scale) and NOT an environment run (all three samples are low-EFE BY CONSTRUCTION: SPARC Y in [1.1e-07, 1.9e-05], HI field dwarfs g_ext ~ 0.001-0.01 a0, MIGHTEE none published, R_efe beyond every ring -- C8): the g_ext axis is VACUOUS in the deep samples.  The run is BETWEEN samples (selection and photometric-mass systematics: MIGHTEE's resolved-SED Upsilon_star vs SPARC's 3.6-micron 0.5-0.6 -- G133's systematics budget, which marches MIGHTEE onto the RAR band but never onto the DE scale) plus the registered sub-DE SPARC deep slope (G183: per-galaxy deep beta = 0.601 +- 0.031 -> n = 1.20 +- 0.06).
  [PASS] V3 [honest statement] stated   V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT.  The specific G189 claim is CONFIRMED: the MIGHTEE deep end reads s_Lambda = 2 a0_DE (deep-only refit 1.8745e-10 = 1.00113 x s_Lambda, reproducing the registered 0.12%; full deep-90% fit 1.9000e-10 at +0.1 sigma, C4).  The UNIVERSAL extension FAILS with the numbers: the pooled per-system deep ratio reads eta = 0.853 (-2.3 sigma below the seesaw line, N = 76), because the deep end is NOT one constant -- SPARC reads 0.616 x s_Lambda (-3.7 sigma, SUB-DE), HI reads 0.774 x (fit) / 0.777 x (eta median, R-free a0_eff = 0.574 x s_Lambda), and only MIGHTEE reads it (1.015 x).  The SEE-saw does NOT return through the deep limit: the one-constant framework is restored at the deep end for the MIGHTEE (HI-selected, resolved-SED) class ONLY, and the deep-limit a0_eff staircase (SPARC 1.152e-10 < HI 1.448e-10 < MIGHTEE 1.900e-10, x a0_DE) is a 2.96 x spread -- the interpolation's n-trouble is NOT merely a transition-regime story; the deep-limit amplitude itself is sample-dependent, and the between-sample run tracks the SAME systematics G133 quantified on the full staircase (M/L normalization), with the SPARC deep end additionally sub-DE (G183's per-galaxy deep slope n = 1.20 +- 0.06, registered).  What IS universal at the deep end: the DEEP SHAPE (the RAR slope ~ 1/2 per point: the residual scatter of eta is 0.128 dex within MIGHTEE and the per-galaxy MADs are 0.1-0.2 dex -- the deep law is a law, its NORMALIZATION is the sample-dependent quantity: s_Lambda (= 2 a0_DE) is the MIGHTEE-class scale, RAR-class for HI, sub-DE for SPARC).

